  "body": "## Summary\n\nDependent draft after #389. Removes arbitrary exception contents from payment-event and merchandise-reservation worker logs, and prevents synchronous diagnostic-output failures from terminating any of the three commerce workers. No financial state transition, provider activation, production deployment or API/client change.\n\n- Preserve fixed component/level/message diagnostics and integer-only information counters; retain idle behavior.\n- Never render exceptions into log events. The old character-stripping helper was not credential/PII redaction and could produce invalid JSON.\n- Isolate diagnostic sink failures without repeating a payment/expiry tick, changing leases or suppressing asynchronous cancellation.\n- Add 24 regression examples, including three generated-text properties, at the actual production iteration boundaries.\n- Preserve latest observed main and reuse the single-token documentation cleanup from #392; do not duplicate that patch or expose its old value.\n- Add ADR 0127, exact test evidence, threat-model limits and an operational runbook.\n\n## Dependencies and review order\n\nBase: #389 / `codex/payment-stack-integration-20260915`. Existing payment stack through #389 first; preserve #392's cleanup as part of this history. Main `3763a407146874a09095e26303a999f5a348afd1` and #392 `2455951713967642de9b429c5a790ceec6cb1fa2` are included through local integration commits. No GitHub PR was merged.\n\nThe comparison includes main's already-reviewed #355 social formal artifacts because the base has older main ancestry. New runtime changes are confined to `ProviderEventWorker.hs`, `MerchReservationWorker.hs` and `ProviderReconciliation.hs`; test registration adds `WorkerLoggingSpec.hs`. Catalog reports are generated with the unchanged 1,135 reviewed decisions; no authority or feature gate weakened.\n\nMobile remains unchanged at #82 / `33720ef45b0565005c4b54b0e0c106cc93831613`; generated web/mobile contracts compare byte-identically. No UI change or screenshot.\n\n## Executed local verification\n\nLocal macOS, Node 24.8, Stack lts-24.42/GHC 9.10.3, PostgreSQL 16.10. Synthetic exception markers and provider fixtures only, not a real sandbox.\n\n- Final runtime/test source `9e28364fa3d24d6d91fa5d7405723b39ba69c32c`: **24 targeted examples / zero failures**, including 300 generated exception-text cases; **2,627 full backend examples / zero failures**, exit 0, 2026-09-16 03:47 UTC.\n- Behavioral-fix source `e19de03981b4d91fcd7f017aef14dfef93f16edf`: **215 PostgreSQL examples / zero failures**, whole harness exit 0 including repeat migration, empty rollback/operator-seed retention, reapply and used-history rollback refusal. The only later source change wraps four fixed log literals; final targeted/full checks repeated after that cleanup.\n- **232 repository tests**, exit 0; formal checks: zero critical/errors, existing 377 warnings / 9,387 informational findings retained.\n- Final catalog: **1,432 files / 1,135 reviewed candidates**, JSON and CSV gates exit 0; no unreviewed/stale decisions. Relative documentation links, generated-client comparison and whitespace checks passed.\n\nRetained negative evidence: initial selection command had a quoting error and ran no tests. Corrected pre-fix run had **24 examples / 10 failures** (log content/encoding, exception rendering and unavailable sinks). Those assertions now pass unchanged. An initial local merge commit was made before catalog regeneration finished; it was corrected/amended while unpublished and never pushed with conflict markers. Existing compiler/module/linker advisories remain documented.\n\nThe only disposable PostgreSQL server was stopped and independently verified stopped; synthetic data/logs retained. Commands, timestamps, source commits and local log paths:\n[worker diagnostic evidence](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/codex/payment-worker-log-safety-20260915/docs/payments/worker-log-safety-2026-09-15.md).\n\n## Operations, rollback and limitations\n\nNo SQL migration/backfill, schema/client change, new configuration flag, provider call or financial mutation. Diagnose through fixed event metadata, authorized queue/reconciliation views and independent log-delivery/queue-age monitoring. A failed log never authorizes an immediate provider retry. Financial audit writes retain their existing failure semantics; no durable diagnostic sink or worker heartbeat is added.\n\nPrefer a forward repair; binary rollback reintroduces log exposure and worker-exit risk. Preserve queues, original attempts, provider references, audit/history and existing payment holds. Do not restore raw exception logging or clear financial data to investigate.\n\nTwo staging inspector attempts (including approved unrestricted retry) again returned HTTP 200 health but all six hosting checks unavailable, `sourceCommit=null`, `providerQualified=false`. Restore authorized `FLY_STAGING_API_TOKEN` / `FLY_STAGING_WEB_TOKEN` or local Fly login before deployed-SHA, merchant sandbox and webhook qualification. No credential values were displayed or used for a provider request.\n\n#392 removes a signing-secret-shaped example from the current document, **not Git history or a configured credential**. If the old example was ever installed, authorized exposure assessment and rotation remain necessary. No credential validity, rotation or Stripe Ecuador eligibility is claimed.\n\nNo provider sandbox, qualified staging, native/device/manual QA, external log-service or deployed shutdown test. Remaining recurring/refund/void/product-fulfillment and compliant seller-settlement/payout flows, legal/accounting/PCI review and production activation remain open. This is not completion of the full payment platform.\n",
